From 73578d6066ef0bd44380fe0fb78d1eae46607418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christoph Berliner <32103696+Styx85@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:43:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] rocblas/tensile: fall back to the generic code-object
 family library

When no Tensile library exists for the exact GPU architecture (e.g. gfx90c,
the Vega APU in Renoir/Cezanne), rocBLAS aborted with 'Cannot read
TensileLibrary_lazy_gfx90c.dat' although the gfx9-generic library, whose
code objects the runtime can load on gfx90c, is installed.

- rocBLAS: look up the library for the exact architecture first, then for
  its LLVM generic family (gfx9-generic, gfx9-4-generic, gfx10-1-generic,
  gfx10-3-generic, gfx11-generic, gfx12-generic). The selected architecture
  is used for the library path, the code object glob and the helper kernel
  code object; library maps stay keyed by the hardware architecture.
- Tensile: do not append the hardware architecture to a fallback library
  prefix that already ends in an architecture suffix (e.g.
  ..._fallback_gfx9-generic), which produced a non-existent
  ..._fallback_gfx9-generic_gfx90c.hsaco.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 projects/rocblas/library/src/tensile_host.cpp | 132 ++++++++++++------
 .../include/Tensile/PlaceholderLibrary.hpp    |  17 +--
 2 files changed, 97 insertions(+), 52 deletions(-)

diff --git a/projects/rocblas/library/src/tensile_host.cpp b/projects/rocblas/library/src/tensile_host.cpp
